      "issue": "The draft attributes the actions in the cancer story to 'Kim Scott's actions when her employee's father was diagnosed.' The evidence (S1:E5–S1:E9) clearly indicates Kim Scott is the recipient of the care, not the provider. Excerpt S1:E5 states 'She cared personally,' and S1:E8 quotes the boss saying 'Kim, look, you go to the airport.' The draft reverses the roles, incorrectly identifying Kim Scott as the boss who sent the employee home, whereas the text shows Kim Scott was the employee who was sent home by her boss."
